1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,700
Why is the area of a circle πr²?
(Last time: circumference = 2πr)

2
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:06,800
Cut the circle into equal slices, like a pizza.

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,500
Fit them together, alternating up and down...

4
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:14,500
The thinner the slices, the closer it gets to a rectangle!

5
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:19,300
Width = half the circumference = 2πr ÷ 2 = πr
Height = the radius, r

6
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:22,800
Area of a rectangle = width × height
πr × r = πr²

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:26,900
π × radius × radius — that's the area of a circle!
